  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase-out of HCFC-22 in the room and unitary air-conditioning equipment manufacturing sector of Argentina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target of this particular project (which is a component of the whole HPMP) was the elimination of 53.46 tons ODP by converting several plants in Argentina (9 companies)  HCFC-22 is used in the manufacture of room and unitary air-conditioner products. All room air conditioner manufacturers are located in the special industrial development zone in the Province of Tierra del Fuego, Ant&#x251c;&#xed;rtida e Islas del Atl&#x251c;&#xed;ntico Sur.  One company producing unitary air conditioning equipment for commercial and industrial buildings is located in Buenos Aires.  Impact of project on Country#s Montreal Protocol Obligations Immediate impact of the project is to phase-out the use of 972 MT of HCFC-22 by converting to HFC refrigeration technology, thereby contributing to the country#s obligation to freeze the HCFC consumption by 2013 and to reduce it by 10% by 2015.  The enterprises# HCFC-22 consumption is significant compared to the country#s total HCFC consumption, and it is expected that the reduction by this project may comprise the major part of the country#s reduction obligation in 2015.</narrative>
  </description>
